    "skewness_raw": 6.5269,
    "skewness_log": 0.0455,
    "p99_to_p50_ratio_raw": 129.2,
    "commentary": "WRTN_PREM_AMT is highly right-skewed (skewness = 6.5269). The p99/p50 ratio of 129.2 illustrates the extreme right tail: the 99th-percentile row writes roughly 129x more premium than the median row. A small fraction of agency-product-state-year cells dominate the variance in raw dollars. log(WRTN_PREM_AMT + 1) reduces skewness to 0.0455, compressing the right tail and producing a distribution that is far more consistent with OLS assumptions (near-symmetric, stabilized variance). Modeling raw WRTN_PREM_AMT directly would violate OLS homoskedasticity: residual variance would grow with fitted values across the premium range. The log transform is strongly justified as the primary specification. Raw-dollar modeling is not recommended but could be explored as a sensitivity check after the log-scale model is established, or as a comparison using a robust or quantile regression."
  }
